{
  "info": {
    "name": "Meu Carrinho API (local)",
    "_postman_id": "5b0c0a52-3c1e-4f0a-9d9e-6a1f2b3c4d5e",
    "description": "Local testing against `make run` (API on :8080, demo seed, mock-oauth2 on :8090).\n\nSign-in is automatic: the collection's pre-request script asks mock-oauth2 for a token for the `user` collection variable (marina, jessica or onias from the seed; any other name is a brand-new user who must call **Me › Sign up / refresh (PUT /v1/me)** first). Change `user` to switch people.\n\nList writes need `If-Match`; the collection's test script copies each response's ETag into `etag`, and the last list and item you touched into `listId` and `itemId`. Start with **Lists › Active lists**, then **Lists › Get list**.\n\nSee RUNNING.md.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Fetches a token from mock-oauth2 for {{user}} whenever none is held, it expired, or {{user}} changed.",
          "const user = pm.variables.get('user');",
          "const expiresAt = Number(pm.collectionVariables.get('tokenExpiresAt') || 0);",
          "if (pm.collectionVariables.get('token') && pm.collectionVariables.get('tokenUser') === user && Date.now() < expiresAt) {",
          "    return;",
          "}",
          "pm.sendRequest({",
          "    url: pm.variables.get('authUrl') + '/default/token',",
          "    method: 'POST',",
          "    header: { 'Content-Type': 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded' },",
          "    body: { mode: 'urlencoded', urlencoded: [",
          "        { key: 'grant_type', value: 'client_credentials' },",
          "        { key: 'client_id', value: user },",
          "        { key: 'client_secret', value: 'local' },",
          "        { key: 'scope', value: 'carrinho-api' }",
          "    ] }",
          "}, (err, res) => {",
          "    if (err || res.code !== 200) {",
          "        console.error('No token from mock-oauth2. Is it running? Try `make deps`.', err || res.text());",
          "        return;",
          "    }",
          "    const body = res.json();",
          "    pm.collectionVariables.set('token', body.access_token);",
          "    pm.collectionVariables.set('tokenUser', user);",
          "    pm.collectionVariables.set('tokenExpiresAt', String(Date.now() + (body.expires_in - 60) * 1000));",
          "});"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Keeps {{etag}} and {{listId}} on the last list you touched, and {{itemId}} on the last item you added.",
          "const etag = pm.response.headers.get('ETag');",
          "if (etag) { pm.collectionVariables.set('etag', etag); }",
          "let body = null;",
          "try { body = pm.response.json(); } catch (e) { body = null; }",
          "if (body && Array.isArray(body.items) && body.version !== undefined) {",
          "    pm.collectionVariables.set('listId', body.id);",
          "    const path = pm.request.url.getPath();",
          "    const added = pm.request.method === 'POST' && (/\\/items$/.test(path) || /\\/items\\/[^/]+\\/duplicate$/.test(path));",
          "    const unset = !pm.collectionVariables.get('itemId') || !body.items.some(i => i.id === pm.collectionVariables.get('itemId'));",
          "    if ((added || (unset && pm.request.method === 'GET')) && body.items.length) {",
          "        pm.collectionVariables.set('itemId', body.items[body.items.length - 1].id);",
          "    }",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
